        "Note",
        "<strong>Adonijah’s coup.</strong> Adonijah is the eldest surviving son after Amnon, Absalom, and Chileab. By Near Eastern primogeniture he is the natural heir, and his support base — Joab the long-time general and Abiathar the priest — represents the old guard from David’s wilderness years. The opposing faction (Nathan, Zadok, Benaiah) belongs to David’s later, Jerusalem-based establishment. The coup narrative is, at one level, a struggle between two halves of David’s career.",
