        "walk before me in truth",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        '<strong>The conditional clause.</strong> David’s charge to Solomon recasts the Davidic covenant of 2 Sam 7 with an "if" attached: <em>if</em> your sons walk faithfully, the throne will not lack a man. Deuteronomistic theology runs through this hinge — the unconditional dynastic promise of 2 Sam 7:13–16 is here subjected to a conditional reading, framing the entire Kings narrative. The historian who shaped this material (the "Deuteronomist" of mainstream scholarship) treats the exile as the explanatory verdict on this conditionality: the dynasty failed the test, and the historian shows how.',
        "User original",
