        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Marriage to Pharaoh’s daughter.</strong> First mention of Solomon’s foreign marriages, foreshadowing the apostasy of ch. 11. Egyptian sources do not record any pharaoh giving a daughter to a foreign king during this period — Egyptian princesses were almost never sent abroad — so historians have long debated the report’s literal accuracy. Some propose she was a minor royal woman; others read the marriage as schematic, lending Solomon international stature.",
        "User original",
