        "Note",
        "Note",
        '<strong>Dream-revelation at Gibeon.</strong> Incubation oracles — sleeping at a sanctuary to receive divine communication — are well attested across the ancient Near East (Mari, Egypt, Mesopotamia). Gibeon was a major "high place" before the temple’s centralization; the narrative legitimizes Solomon’s worship there as transitional, before Jerusalem becomes the single sanctuary.',
