        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Ark brought into the temple.</strong> The cloud filling the temple (vv. 10-11) consciously echoes Exodus 40:34-35 at the wilderness Tabernacle. Yahweh’s presence has migrated from desert to city. The narrator stages this as the climax of the entire conquest-monarchy arc: from Sinai through the wilderness, the conquest, the judges, and David’s wars — to a settled house for the Name.",
