        "I will surely tear the kingdom from you",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        '<strong>The kingdom’s tearing.</strong> The verb <em>qara\'</em> ("tear") will recur in 11:30 when Ahijah tears his garment into twelve pieces and gives ten to Jeroboam — a prophetic enactment of the political tearing this verse announces. The Davidic dynasty will retain only Judah and (formally) Benjamin; the ten northern tribes will go to Jeroboam. The tearing-language reverses the consolidation Solomon achieved at his coronation in chapter 2. What David won by force, Solomon kept by wisdom, then lost by syncretism.',
        "User original",
