        "the book of the acts of Solomon",
        "source",
        "Variant",
        "Variant",
        '<strong>The lost source.</strong> The Kings narrator regularly cites his sources: "the book of the acts of Solomon" here, "the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel/Judah" throughout. None of these source documents survive. The narrator’s frequent citation of them is a small window onto Israelite scribal practice — the Deuteronomistic historian worked with palace records, prophetic traditions, and northern and southern royal annals, fusing them into the present narrative. Modern source-criticism descends from attempts to detect the seams between these underlying documents.',
        "User original",
