        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Jeroboam’s golden calves.</strong> The Deuteronomist condemns Jeroboam unforgivably for the bull-images at Bethel and Dan, repeating the verdict throughout Kings (’the sin of Jeroboam son of Nebat’). Some scholars argue the bulls may have functioned as pedestals for the invisible Yahweh — directly parallel to the cherubim throne in Jerusalem — and so were not idolatrous in original conception. The Deuteronomistic editor allows no such nuance.",
