        "Note",
        "<strong>Omri.</strong> Twelve verses for one of the most powerful Israelite kings. For more than a century after his death, Assyrian inscriptions refer to the northern kingdom as bīt Ḫumri (’House of Omri’). The Mesha Stele (c. 840 BCE, Moabite) describes Omri’s hegemony over Moab. The Deuteronomist deliberately compresses his account, downplaying achievements that fall outside the cultic evaluation framework.",
        "User original",
