        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Ahab and Jezebel.</strong> The Sidonian alliance through Jezebel imports Tyrian Baal worship at the state level. The Tel Dan Aramaic inscription (c. 840 BCE) likely references Joram son of Ahab and ’Ahaziahu, king of the house of David’ — the earliest extra-biblical reference to David’s dynasty. The Omride dynasty’s archaeological footprint (Samaria’s monumental architecture) confirms its political weight.",
        "User original",
