        "Elijah the Tishbite",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Elijah at Cherith.</strong> The name Elijah (’Yahweh is God’) programs the conflict the prophet embodies: Yahweh versus Baal. Drought is the precise instrument of vindication, since Baal is the storm and rain god of Canaan and Phoenicia — Yahweh withholds rain from Baal’s home turf to demonstrate sovereignty over it.",
        "User original",
