        "a handful of meal in the jar",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>The widow of Zarephath.</strong> Yahweh feeds the prophet not in Israelite territory but in Phoenician Sidon — Jezebel’s home country. The provision-from-nothing motif (handful of meal, little oil, neither runs out) parallels Elisha’s widow’s oil (2 Kgs 4:1–7) and is invoked by Jesus in Luke 4:25–26 to make a controversial point: the prophet was sent past the widows of Israel to a foreigner. The crowd’s violent response in Luke 4:28–29 reads against the grain of any easy reading: the universalist edge of Elijah’s ministry is unwelcome.",
        "User original",
