        "seven thousand in Israel",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        '<strong>The remnant.</strong> Elijah’s self-pity ("I, only I, am left") is corrected: Yahweh has preserved seven thousand who have not bowed to Baal. The remnant theology articulated here becomes structural in later prophetic literature (Isa 6:13, 10:20–22) and decisive for Paul in Rom 11:2–5, who quotes this exact verse to argue that Yahweh has not rejected Israel but preserved a remnant. The doctrine of remnant — that fidelity persists invisibly amid apostasy — recurs as a pattern across Jewish and Christian self-understanding in periods of crisis.',
